      "created_at": "2026-10-10T04:05:24Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-10T04:05:24Z",
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "I've expanded the description into a proposal to replace background validation with crowdsourced UTXO snapshot verification through default IBD hash checks, keeping only the latest hash.\nThis extends the existing choice between `-assumevalid=0` and the default to the UTXO starting state, with confidence in its hash coming from routine checks across the network.\nThe hash check would warn on a mismatch without stopping IBD, replacing my original proposal to assert. Snapshot imports would still require the expected UTXO set hash.\nThe update adds local hash timings, the pruning model and optional reindexing, resource and maintenance costs, and the differing views on [P2P snapshot distribution](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/35054).\n",
      "user": {
        "login": "l0rinc",
        "id": 1841944,
        "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDE5NDQ=",
